orm=\"translate(69.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(128 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6c\" transform=\"translate(177.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(216.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(238.015625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(292.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(316.71875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(355.015625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(378.921875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" transform=\"translate(402.828125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" transform=\"translate(461.234375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(519.328125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pbcc498f967\"><rect x=\"24.576719\" y=\"27.296\" width=\"357.12\" height=\"144.144\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Days per stage of a heavy check","note":null},"answer":"<p>Repair time is the same (10 days). The gap is all <b>waiting</b>: parts (9 vs 2 days) and approvals (3 vs 1). SkyLine spends 12 of its 28 days (43%) waiting. (Best airlines spend one extra day on testing.) <b>So-what:</b> this is a planning problem, not a skills problem. Fix parts first: it's 7 of the 8 days.</p>"},{"q":"The team proposes: (1) order parts in advance based on past checks, holding $5M of extra stock (cost of holding stock: 20% a year); (2) digital sign-off software at $0.5M a year. Parts waiting falls to 4 days and approvals to 1. Is it worth it?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Days saved = (9 − 4) + (3 − 1) = <b>7 days</b> → 7 × 20 × $60k = <b>$8.4M/year</b>.</p> <p>Costs = $5M × 20% + $0.5M = <b>$1.5M/year</b>. Net ≈ <b>+$6.9M/year</b>. Clearly worth it.</p>"}],"reco":"SkyLine's heavy checks take 8 days longer than the best airlines because aircraft wait for parts and approvals, not because repairs are slow. Pre-ordering parts and digital sign-off cut 7 days per check, worth $8.4M a year for $1.5M of cost (net ~$6.9M). Start with the next 5 checks, then tackle the 2 extra days still spent waiting for parts (4 vs 2); testing needs no work, as SkyLine is already a day faster than its peers there. Risk: holding parts that don't get used, so review the parts list every quarter.","great":["Sizes the prize first","Separates working time from waiting time","Nets off the cost of holding stock"],"id":9,"slug":"skyline-mro"}